DESCRIPTION:Closing the Hunger Gap is hosting our second event in our new y
 earlong series with a reflective discussion on the Theory of Change! Join u
 s for generative dialogue with leadership team members in the BE group. Clo
 sing the Hunger Gap is a national network of food banks\, pantries\, and ot
 her anti-hunger organizations and advocates. We believe that for all commun
 ities to have access to the food they need and want\, we need a liberated\,
  joyful way of BEING in a beloved community in which all people are free fr
 om oppression\, fully resourced\, and able to truly thrive.<br><br>✅ Readin
 gs from The Serviceberry: Abundance and Reciprocity in the Natural World<br
 >✅ Exercises from Beyond Survival: Strategies and Stories from the Transfor
 mational Justice Movement<br>📅 Thursday\, March 20\, 2025 | 10:00 AM-11:30
  AM PT/ 1-2:30 PM EST<br>📍 Virtual Event | Zoom<br><span>🔗</span><span> <
 /span><span>Register: </span><a href="https://us02web.zoom.us/meeting/regis
 ter/7ktO5LPBQ5KjfY1PZvNw5A#/registration">https://us02web.zoom.us/meeting/r
 egister/7ktO5LPBQ5KjfY1PZvNw5A#/registration</a>
LAST-MODIFIED:20250303T194942Z
LOCATION:Zoom
SEQUENCE:0
STATUS:CONFIRMED
SUMMARY:All Flourishing is Mutual: Strategies for Being in the Food Justice
  Movement
TRANSP:OPAQUE
END:VEVENT
