UID:7q2kr7c4qffbkduhq7k9p2qb3c@google.com
CREATED:20190115T203446Z
DESCRIPTION:Join us for reading and feasting! In collaboration with Monroe 
 County Public Library\, we will be hosting a book club here at Mother Hubba
 rd's Cupboard. Cooking and conversation fueled by a good read is what this 
 book club is all about. Meals will be vegetarian\, vegan and gluten-free fr
 iendly though please let us know if you have any dietary restrictions when 
 registering.<br><br>The book this month will be <i><b>Relish: My Life in th
 e Kitchen by Lucy Knisley</b></i>.<br><br><i>Lucy Knisley loves food. The d
 aughter of a chef and a gourmet\, this talented young cartoonist comes by h
 er obsession honestly. In her forthright\, thoughtful\, and funny memoir\, 
 Lucy traces key episodes in her life thus far\, framed by what she was eati
 ng at the time and lessons learned about food\, cooking\, and life. Each ch
 apter is bookended with an illustrated recipe―many of them treasured family
  dishes\, and a few of them Lucy's original inventions.</i><br><i><br></i><
 br><i>A welcome read for anyone who ever felt more passion for a sandwich t
 han is strictly speaking proper\, Relish is a graphic novel for our time: i
 t invites the reader to celebrate food as a connection to our bodies and a 
 connection to the earth\, rather than an enemy\, a compulsion\, or a consum
 er product.</i><br><br>Books can be checked out at Mother Hubbard's Cupboar
 d or through the library beginning February 18th or ordered through the Boo
 k Corner at (812) 339-1522.&nbsp\;<br><br>Call (812)-355-6843 or e-mail Ali
 ssa at education@mhcfoodpantry.org to register and reserve a book or for mo
 re information.
LAST-MODIFIED:20190115T203510Z
LOCATION:Mother Hubbard's Cupboard\, Bloomington\, IN 47403\, USA
SEQUENCE:1
STATUS:CONFIRMED
SUMMARY:A Readable Feast
TRANSP:OPAQUE
END:VEVENT
